{
 "name": "mourn-keen-bat",
 "issue": "Mourn's keen spawned echo bats at a blind +/-26px offset, so fighting near a wall put a bat INSIDE it (replay: bat at 705,184 in the arena east wall, three columns of stone). The bat could not be fought and collision could not see it. Root cause was a layer down: placeBody returned false — its four shortest-axis passes cannot escape a thick wall — and Monster's constructor ignored the verdict and spawned anyway. placeBody now falls back to a bounded outward search that respects the level extent, Monster refuses to exist when placement fails, and keen calls bats into open air above rather than blindly to the sides.",
